No tsconfig setting alone enables type-checking at build time. `astro dev` and `astro build` transpile with esbuild and skip type checking. To gate releases, change your `build` script in `package.json` to run `astro check` before building:

```json
{
  "scripts": {
    "build": "astro check && astro build"
  }
}
```

`astro check` inspects all files in your TypeScript project (use `svelte-check` or `vue-tsc` for Svelte/Vue files). The build produces a deploy-ready site in `dist/` by default and reports build errors in the terminal.

Docs: https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/typescript/
